 "https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:gmd:gmd403:g4034:g4034f:ct011603/full/pct:25/0/default.jpg#h=685&w=775"], "index": 6, "language": ["english"], "location": ["texas", "united states", "fort worth"], "mime_type": ["image/gif", "image/tiff", "image/jpeg", "image/jp2"], "number": ["75696595", "2025-06-07t18:31:11.100000", "2019-12-09t13:11:34"], "online_format": ["image"], "original_format": ["map"], "partof": ["cities and towns", "catalog", "geography and map division"], "score": 22.043907, "shelf_id": "G4034.F7A3 1914 .H3", "site": ["catalog"], "subject": ["texas", "united states", "fort worth (tex.)", "aerial views", "fort worth"], "timestamp": "2026-04-29T16:17:25.775Z", "title": "Bird's-eye view of Fort Worth, Texas", "type": ["cartographic"], "url": "https://www.loc.gov/item/75696595/"}], "reproductions": "<p>\nSome images in this collection are described in groups; others are \ndescribed individually. In some cases, all of the images in the \ngroup display online, in other cases they do not.\n</p>\n\n<p>\nYou can download online images yourself.  Alternatively, you can \npurchase copies of various types.\n</p>\n\n<ol>\n<p>\t\n<strong><li>Determine whether the desired materials can be retrieved \nonline.</strong>\n</p>\n<ul>\n<p>\t\n<li>Look in the <strong>Medium</strong> field above to determine whether\n the description is for one photograph or more than one.</li>\n </p>\n <p>\n<li>If the description is for a single item and it is displaying, \nyou can download or purchase a print.  Cite the number that begins \nwith &quot;LC-DIG...&quot; when purchasing copies through Library of \nCongress Duplication Services.\n</p>\n<p>\n<li>If the description is for more than one item and there is \na &quot;Click for more images&quot; icon displaying, select that. \nIndividual images will display; you can download or purchase prints. \nCite the number that begins with &quot;LC-DIG...&quot; when purchasing \ncopies through Library of Congress Duplication Services.\n</p>\n<p>\n<li>If the description is for more than one item and there is no\n &quot;Click for more images&quot; icon displaying, return to the\n  &quot;About this Item&quot; tab and select the &quot;<i>Check for \n  online items from this group</i>&quot; link.  Then select the \n  \"Obtaining Copies\" tab for any retrieved items that are of interest.\n</p>\n</ul>\n</li>\n\n<p>\n<strong><li>If the images do not display online</strong> -- Select images for reproduction through one of these methods:\n</p>\n<ul>\n<p>\t\n<li>Visit the Prints &amp; Photographs Reading Room and request to view \nthe group (general information about service in the reading room is \navailable at: <a href=\"//www.loc.gov/rr/print/info/001_ref.html\">https://www.loc.gov/rr/print/info/001_ref.html</a>).</li>  \n</p>\n<p>\n<li>P&amp;P reading room staff can provide up to 15 photocopies of items \nper calendar year. (Color images cannot be photocopied.) For assistance,\n see our <a href=\"//www.loc.gov/rr/askalib/ask-print.html\">Ask a Librarian</a> page. OR</li>\n</p>\n<p>\n<li>Hire a freelance researcher to do further selection for you \n(a list of researchers is available at: \n<a href=\"//www.loc.gov/rr/print/resource/013_pic.html\">https://www.loc.gov/rr/print/resource/013_pic.html</a>).\n</p>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ol>\n\n<p>\n<strong>Purchasing Copies</strong>\n</p>\n\n<p>\nLibrary of Congress Duplication Services can make copies of various \ntypes from images in Prints & Photographs Division Collections.  \nPrice lists, contact information, and order forms are available on the \n<a href=\"//www.loc.gov/duplicationservices/\">Duplication Services Web site</a>.\n</p>\n\n<p>\nCarol M. Highsmith sells prints of her photographs at: <a href=\"http://photographsamerica.com/\">http://photographsamerica.com/</a> .\n</p>  \n\n\n\n\n        ", "resources": [{"caption": "original digital file", "files": [[{"height": 244, "levels": 1, "mimetype": "image/jpeg", "url": "https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:pnp:highsm:18700:18744/full/pct:6.25/0/default.jpg", "width": 307}, {"height": 488, "levels": 1, "mimetype": "image/jpeg", "url": "https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:pnp:highsm:18700:18744/full/pct:12.5/0/default.jpg", "width": 615}, {"height": 976, "levels": 1, "mimetype": "image/jpeg", "url": "https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:pnp:highsm:18700:18744/full/pct:25/0/default.jpg", "width": 1230}, {"height": 1952, "levels": 1, "mimetype": "image/jpeg", "url": "https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:pnp:highsm:18700:18744/full/pct:50/0/default.jpg", "width": 2460}, {"height": 3905, "info": "https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:pnp:highsm:18700:18744/info.json", "levels": 7, "mimetype": "image/jp2", "size": 3912109, "url": "https://tile.loc.gov/storage-services/service/pnp/highsm/18700/18744.jp2", "width": 4920}]], "image": "https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:pnp:highsm:18700:18744/full/pct:6.25/0/default.jpg", "url": "https://www.loc.gov/resource/highsm.18744/"}], "thesaurus_entry": null, "timestamp": 1792527255865, "unrestricted": true}